[{:db/id 17592186172130 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e6c3f387-d028-56cc-8550-337dfde31023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172131 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d41258e7-4727-5661-9adb-26ceb25d76d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6c3f387-d028-56cc-8550-337dfde31023" :question/id #uuid "e6c3f387-d028-56cc-8550-337dfde31023" :question/math-academy-id "q-161135" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xz+y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,-v,\\,-{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xz+y)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=-v\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-{v}^{2})+(-v) \\\\  & =-u{v}^{2}-v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(-u{v}^{2}-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de80caed-f292-5fbc-ae6d-5bf6abf46eda"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de80caed-f292-5fbc-ae6d-5bf6abf46eda" :answer-field/id #uuid "de80caed-f292-5fbc-ae6d-5bf6abf46eda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-059c12fe-eab5-50d3-812e-daede28e5fce" "answer-a69adeb6-2c36-5a75-b29d-f701876ba59a" "answer-e264331f-dc93-54c6-bb93-c8cd29731c14" "answer-ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" "answer-cbbd9a36-5d62-5a45-a0b6-211a1e349cc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-059c12fe-eab5-50d3-812e-daede28e5fce" :answer/id #uuid "059c12fe-eab5-50d3-812e-daede28e5fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-uv-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a69adeb6-2c36-5a75-b29d-f701876ba59a" :answer/id #uuid "a69adeb6-2c36-5a75-b29d-f701876ba59a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}+v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e264331f-dc93-54c6-bb93-c8cd29731c14" :answer/id #uuid "e264331f-dc93-54c6-bb93-c8cd29731c14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" :answer/id #uuid "ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbbd9a36-5d62-5a45-a0b6-211a1e349cc3" :answer/id #uuid "cbbd9a36-5d62-5a45-a0b6-211a1e349cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u{v}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d41258e7-4727-5661-9adb-26ceb25d76d0" :question/id #uuid "d41258e7-4727-5661-9adb-26ceb25d76d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161185" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(xy+xz)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,2v,\\,6v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{10}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xy+xz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=2v\\,z=6v} \\\\  & =(u)(2v)+(u)(6v) \\\\  & =8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8uv\\cdot 2\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}{∬}_{D}\\,uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}({\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u)({\\int }_{0}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}v) \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}\\cdot {[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =16\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ec0f1fd-a976-5791-b23e-66968bb1089c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ec0f1fd-a976-5791-b23e-66968bb1089c" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec0f1fd-a976-5791-b23e-66968bb1089c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10989bff-b98e-51af-bb4a-b28350a226e5" "answer-60f276b3-36f3-5fbe-9d10-b5fec8b429a0" "answer-3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" "answer-b1865271-a8a9-5f44-b938-a958ba7e5f06" "answer-1687e4a9-1caf-5ff9-a03a-04a61daf8637"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10989bff-b98e-51af-bb4a-b28350a226e5" :answer/id #uuid "10989bff-b98e-51af-bb4a-b28350a226e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60f276b3-36f3-5fbe-9d10-b5fec8b429a0" :answer/id #uuid "60f276b3-36f3-5fbe-9d10-b5fec8b429a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" :answer/id #uuid "3d279b80-6077-585e-b090-d7cf3aa7efe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1865271-a8a9-5f44-b938-a958ba7e5f06" :answer/id #uuid "b1865271-a8a9-5f44-b938-a958ba7e5f06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1687e4a9-1caf-5ff9-a03a-04a61daf8637" :answer/id #uuid "1687e4a9-1caf-5ff9-a03a-04a61daf8637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172378 :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=6-3u-2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,6-3u-2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =4xy\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=6-3u-2v} \\\\  & =4uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 3},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot 4\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =36\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186169131 :answer-field/correct 17592186169133 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}]
